  "reference_protocol": "Compare complete SQL statements in both public file modes against SQLite 3.53.4, including output/return code/errors and persisted catalog/rowids/rows/integrity. Correlated declarations come from real bound schemas; scalar collation non-inheritance is a maintained negative control.",
  "implementation": "Membership requests retain explicit and effective/default collation separately. Prepared RHS metadata is derived after actual declaration and lexical-parent binding, using the existing result-collation planner. The comparison resolver chooses explicit LHS, explicit RHS, declared LHS, then declared RHS. BINARY result compounds can run even when their source table has an unrelated non-BINARY field; declared-result compounds remain a separate admission limit.",
  "negative_semantic_control": "The pinned oracle confirms that a scalar SELECT result does not inherit its inner declared or explicit projection collation for an outer comparison. This behavior is preserved and tested; IN query comparison metadata is handled separately rather than applying a general scalar-inheritance rule.",
  "proof_scope": "Registered component equations choose an explicit RHS collation before either default and a declared LHS before a declared RHS. A runtime unit group tests these priorities and scalar-result isolation. Existing generic scalar-query proof claims remain. No full SQL membership-equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and fresh-seed survey share named families and one generator. Their 14 failures are not a global compatibility percentage.",
